==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|nay-sayer}}

===Etymology===
Origin: 1715–1725<!--http://dictionary.reference.com/browse/naysayer -->, from {{affix|en|nay|say|-er}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|naysay|er}}. First recorded use: 1721<!--http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/naysayer -->.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈneɪ.ˌseɪ.ə(ɹ)/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈneɪ.ˌseɪ.ɚ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-naysayer.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|nay|say|er}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who consistently [[denies]], [[criticizes]], or [[doubts]]; a [[detractor]].
#: ''He ignored the '''naysayers''' and succeeded with his idea.''

